1
00:00:00,815 --> 00:00:03,155
(Sheldon(entering):)Looking out at your fresh young faces...

2
00:00:03,318 --> 00:00:06,608
(Sheldon(entering):)...I remember when I too
was deciding my academic future...

3
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:09,570
(Sheldon(entering):)...as a lowly graduate student.

4
00:00:09,741 --> 00:00:12,031
(Sheldon(entering):)Of course, I was 14...

5
00:00:12,494 --> 00:00:14,994
...and had achieved more
than you could ever hope to...

6
00:00:15,163 --> 00:00:17,413
...despite my 9:00 bedtime.

7
00:00:18,625 --> 00:00:22,755
(Sheldon(entering):)Now, there may be one or two of you
in this room who has what it takes...

8
00:00:22,921 --> 00:00:25,051
(Sheldon(entering):)...to succeed in theoretical physics.

9
00:00:25,215 --> 00:00:28,675
It's more likely that you will spend
your careers teaching fifth graders...

10
00:00:28,843 --> 00:00:32,303
...how to make papier-mâché volcanoes
with baking-soda lava.

11
00:00:34,099 --> 00:00:35,349
(Leonard:)Oh, good God.

12
00:00:35,517 --> 00:00:38,647
(Sheldon:)In short, anyone who told you
that you would someday be able...

13
00:00:38,812 --> 00:00:42,192
(Sheldon:)...to make any significant contribution
to physics played a trick on you.

14
00:00:42,357 --> 00:00:44,107
(Sheldon:)A cruel trick indeed.

15
00:00:46,820 --> 00:00:48,030
(Sheldon:)Any questions?

16
00:00:51,157 --> 00:00:53,247
(Sheldon:)Of course not.

17
00:00:54,536 --> 00:00:56,166
(Sheldon:)I weep for the future of science.

18
00:00:56,329 --> 00:00:59,329
(Sheldon:)Now, if you'll excuse me,
the latest issue of Batman is out.

19
00:01:00,375 --> 00:01:01,875
(Sheldon:)Come, Leonard.

20
00:01:05,213 --> 00:01:09,023
(Leonard:)Laser demonstration's looking
pretty good now, huh?

